# Mounted-cert front door for Agora — the ONION / static-cert variant of the BAKED-IN deploy/proxy/Caddyfile.
# Select it by mounting this file OVER the baked Caddyfile at /etc/caddy/Caddyfile: uncomment the mount in
# docker-compose.prod.yml (proxy service), or set CADDYFILE=./deploy/proxy/Caddyfile.onion in the dev compose.
#
# WHY a separate file: the default Caddyfile uses automatic ACME (Let's Encrypt), which CANNOT issue
# for a `.onion` address (no HTTP-01/DNS-01 path). This variant instead serves a cert you supply at
# startup — Caddy uses it as-is and never attempts ACME. Drop your cert + key in the certs dir mounted
# at /certs (host default ./deploy/proxy/certs, override with CADDY_CERTS_DIR) as `site.pem` + `site.key`.
#
# Identical routing — it imports the SAME (agora-site) snippet (serves the SPA + routes every service),
# so there is no routing duplication between this and Caddyfile.
#
# Tor wiring: put the hidden-service address in SERVER_NAME and map the onion's :443 to this proxy, e.g.
#   HiddenServicePort 443 <caddy-host>:443
# so the onion's TLS port reaches Caddy's TLS listener. (Tor already encrypts the transport; the cert
# gives browsers a real secure context — required for secure-chat's WebCrypto outside Tor Browser.)
#
# ONE proxy hop now (just Caddy), so set RATE_LIMIT_TRUSTED_HOPS=1 in .env.

# Loads the (agora-site) snippet — BAKED into the image at /etc/caddy/agora-routes.caddy, so the onion
# variant only needs to mount THIS file (over the Caddyfile) + the certs, not the snippet.
import agora-routes.caddy

{$SERVER_NAME} {
	# Serve the operator-supplied cert + key (mounted read-only at /certs). No ACME is attempted for an
	# explicit `tls <cert> <key>` — issuance/renewal is YOUR responsibility (rotate the files + reload).
	tls /certs/site.pem /certs/site.key

	import agora-site
}
